=== J1: the scale-covariance no-go (exact, sympy) ===
  X_L(y;a0) = (sqrt(1 + 4 a0/y) - 1)/2
  (i)  X_L(lam*y ; lam*a0) - X_L(y;a0) = 0        -> covariance: True
  (ii) g X (1+X) simplifies to: a0              -> exact: True
       under lam: (lam g) X' (1+X') / (g X (1+X)) = lam   (weight 1, relation preserved)
  (iii) F3 (universality: one a_0 for all galaxies/epochs): a_0 -> lam a_0 preserves it.
  (iv) budget: rho_ph = X rho_b carries no a_0 -- invariant.

  F2 (a_0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_*)) is the ONLY relation that is not invariant:
      it DEFINES kappa, so under G_lam:  kappa -> lam * kappa.
      There is no G_lam-invariant left that could fix kappa: X is fixed, M_b fixed,
      rho_* fixed, c,G fixed. kappa is the coordinate ALONG the orbit -> a flat direction.

  [PASS] J1 -- NO-GO CONFIRMED: G_lam is an exact symmetry of F1/F3/every formation relation and kappa is its only charged quantity
        covariance of X_L: True | exact quadratic g X(1+X) = a0: True | weight: lam

