=== J3: the GF1/GF2 n = 2 hook (graded) ===
  certified identity: kappa := a_0/s, s := n a_0  =>  kappa = 1/n; kappa = 1/2 <=> n = 2

  (i)  a_0/(n a_0) - 1/n = 0   -> theorem holds: True
  (ii) GF1 battery at n = 2 (committed numbers):
        germ ratio  = 4.000406   (n^2 = 4)          rel = 1.01e-04
        Z^2         = 33.510322   (32 pi/3 = 33.510322)   rel = 1.08e-08
        Omega_L     = 0.685
        S(n=2)      = 3/2 - ln 2 = 0.806853 (committed)
        -> germ ratio and S are a_0-free; Z^2 is a_0-bearing. n = 2 IS pinned by an
           a_0-free channel (germ/S).  (ii) = YES

  (iii) kappa = a_0/s fixes the RATIO a_0/s only. Substituting into F2 gives
          s = a_0/kappa = c sqrt(G rho_*),
        i.e. the identification s = c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) IS the statement F2 with kappa = 1/n.
        kappa = 1/n is therefore silent about which rho_* stands under the root; it
        constrains the shape/normalisation of the RESPONSE, not the cosmic density.
        -> (iii) = NO.

  [FAIL] J3 -- J3 = RESTATEMENT, not a formation output: kappa = 1/n is a theorem (i) and n = 2 is measured a_0-free (ii), but the rho_Lambda identification is F2 itself (iii)
        the n = 2 channel transports the EXPONENT/INDEX; it does not select the cosmic density, and it is not formation physics

